# Complete frozen H25 qualification with native GF(2)

The fixed six-run comparison reduced median wall time **27.84%**, from **39.686181760 to 28.636256246 seconds**, and median CPU **28.09%**, from **39.58 to 28.46 seconds**. Both reductions pass the predeclared 15% and within-arm-spread gates. This measures the complete frozen historical `complex_network.py` H25 CLI **with retained exact observations**, including cold source copies, custody checks, imports and serialization. Every candidate additionally pays compilation/link/load and all unchanged independent finite controls.

This is not a bare-CLI performance factor, a current selected-frontier replay, a new mathematical construction or κ, or a gain on the separate unresolved PR5864 objective. Hosted correctness checks do not reproduce the local performance factor.

## Complete caller and exact retained outputs

The caller remains byte-identical to canonical main `19fdb086ea96af9a9f87936a2b888e10af4ed810`. It executes its original side-map, label and role checks, network counts, logarithm enclosure, saving comparison, parameters, guard/recurrence/constraint/margin checks, dyadic/ceiling checks, real upstream source verification and gate bound. The actual CLI writes its original certificate and prints both original lines. No source-verifier stub or stored PASS substitutes for execution.

The 32-file closure includes twelve scientific scripts, the upstream manifest and its nineteen payloads. The pinned manuscript commit is `adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a`. The seven native-engine files are unchanged from the historical PR5929 side verification work. The full driver checks source bytes, import identities, runtime bindings, before/after modes and the exact output-file set. Original full-call assertions remain enabled.

All six runs matched the entire certificate, stdout, typed full return, ordered side witness, rank transcript and complement receipt. The typed representation retains exact Fraction pairs, primitive/container type distinctions and dictionary order. It contains no replacement approximate arithmetic. Observations cover **59,959 rank calls, 252 distinct matrices and 238,685 ordered complement calls**. The canonical complement-stream digest represents 55,839,507 observed bytes; the stored complement artifact is its complete receipt, not the stream itself.

## Fixed experiment and failures

| Sample, in executed order | Wall seconds | CPU seconds |
|---|---:|---:|
| B1 | 42.103671320 | 41.64 |
| C1 | 28.636256246 | 28.46 |
| C2 | 28.595429725 | 28.44 |
| B2 | 39.355439922 | 39.28 |
| B3 | 39.686181760 | 39.58 |
| C3 | 33.129227289 | 31.92 |

The slower C3 is retained. Median savings of 11.049925514 wall seconds and 11.12 CPU seconds exceed maximum within-arm spreads of 4.533797564 and 3.48 seconds. See [COMPLETE-GATE.json](evidence/COMPLETE-GATE.json) and the complete [run receipts](evidence/runs/).

Profile v1 failed during import because its entry filename shadowed the standard-library `profile` module. Its error is preserved. A separate entry-name repair left the scientific driver unchanged; profile v2 established the anchor and is excluded from sample selection. There were no benchmark rerolls or automatic retries. Eight original guarded commands, including those two profile attempts, cost about 253.41 seconds under the unchanged serial 180-second/1-GiB policy. Coarse phase measurements are nested diagnostics and must not be added as independent savings.

The local bad-input checkpoint `bb01abd…` is retained only as failed preparation evidence. The actual publication input ancestor is **`7f9c2985de167e95d159040eee26fc03c1e27fb6`**, containing exactly 42 added inputs. No source pin requires unmerged PR5929 history.

## Portable checks and replay

Use Linux CPython 3.12 with existing `cc` and Python headers. The unchanged guard additionally uses `/usr/bin/python3.12` and GNU `/usr/bin/time`. No package installation is requested.

```sh
python3.12 -B research/gf2-full-network/verify.py
python3.12 -B -O research/gf2-full-network/verify.py
python3.12 -B research/gf2-full-network/verify_full.py
python3.12 -B research/gf2-full-network/check_artifacts.py
```

The first two commands execute the unchanged finite dense-oracle, exact-order/type/width/iterator, fallback and runtime-binding controls, using a fresh external build. Failed evidence is retained at its reported path. Optimization is deliberate only for finite controls. `verify_full.py` performs one complete candidate correctness run with original assertions, an inner 150-second guard and a 180-second registered timeout; it never reports a hosted speed factor or adds a benchmark sample. Source/engine inputs remain read-only; only new external runtime directories are writable. `CODE-SOURCES.json` authenticates executable wrappers and frozen inputs before work. Dynamic publication status and evidence metadata are separately declared.

Canonical transport comprises six payloads with **60,831,231 logical bytes**. The checker streams the large witness and rank files, authenticates their complete decompressed bytes against the immutable anchor, checks typed-return structure, and checks the literal reference certificate/stdout and complement receipt. Compressed transport hashes preserve archive identity; regenerated compression is not mathematical identity. See [canonical manifest](evidence/canonical/MANIFEST.json) and [VALIDATION.json](VALIDATION.json) for current check status.

The reported six samples measure `full_driver.py` under the frozen parent guard. Publication wrappers additionally authenticate the archived evidence; their correctness replays are separate checks and do not replace those samples or establish a new wrapper performance factor.

For an explicitly requested new complete replay, use `replay.py B|C NEW_EXTERNAL_DIRECTORY`. It serializes calls for this package, runs the unchanged guard with a 180-second limit and 1-GiB sampled group RSS cap, retains failure evidence and never retries. New timing receipts do not replace the fixed experiment.

## Open next questions

The scoped full historical caller evaluation is complete. Broader caller integration or another interpreter/runtime requires its own source-bound full contract and paid checks before any performance transfer. No additional parameter search, mathematical construction or timing reroll is authorized by this package. Structured scope and blockers are in [TASK.json](TASK.json).

## Credit and limits

Chris R / Clear1nsight with substantial OpenAI Codex and user-requested Astra xhigh assistance; separate agents performed source design and independent static review, with one parent owning all serial scientific execution. Author self-checks are not independent review or human/kernel acceptance. Preserve [PR5929](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/5929), the original CrocSwap/P104 authors and source-specific notices. Packed GF(2) elimination is a standard technique, not a novelty claim. Original upstream license/README are retained under `frozen/upstream/`.

The unchanged engine supports its exact 64-bit domain and original fallback behavior with stable source, builtins and dispatch. This is not abi3, free-threaded/subinterpreter support, a general C-memory-safety proof or formal verification of the multiplication theorem. Historical certificate status and inherited assumptions remain intact.
